<Bindings>
    <!--
      Picked up automatically by the client from the addon's folder: Bindings.xml is never
      listed in the .toc, and listing it there would load it twice. The readable names the
      Key Bindings panel shows come from BINDING_HEADER_DEMONHUNTER and the two
      BINDING_NAME_* globals, set at the bottom of Core.lua.

      (No double hyphen appears anywhere in this comment on purpose: XML forbids it inside a
      comment, and a Bindings.xml the parser rejects is a Bindings.xml the client silently
      drops.)

      THESE BODIES ARE NOT HOW THE SPELL IS CAST, and they cannot be.

      A binding body defined by an addon is addon code, so it runs tainted, and every cast
      entry point the client has is protected. What actually casts is an OVERRIDE binding
      installed by Movement.lua:

          SetOverrideBindingClick(owner, true, key, "DemonHunterDoubleJumpButton", "LeftButton")

      A priority override binding wins over the normal binding for the same key, so while the
      override is installed the body below never runs at all. It runs only when the override
      is MISSING, which is exactly the case worth telling the player about, because the one
      way it happens is a key bound (or a /reload done) during combat, when
      SetOverrideBindingClick is unavailable. So each body is a diagnostic rather than a
      fallback action: it explains why nothing happened instead of leaving a dead key.
    -->
    <Binding name="DEMONHUNTER_DOUBLE_JUMP" header="DEMONHUNTER">
        DemonHunterMovement_BindingPressed("doublejump")
    </Binding>
    <Binding name="DEMONHUNTER_GLIDE">
        DemonHunterMovement_BindingPressed("glide")
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
